Article 4 (Submission and Approval of Research Plans) A person who intends to receive research expenses for research on unification and North Korean issues (hereinafter referred to as "research expenses") shall submit to the President of the National Institute for Peaceful Unification and Democratic Education a research plan containing the following matters (hereinafter referred to as a "research plan"), in accordance with the procedures prescribed by the President of the Institute, and obtain approval thereof. The same shall apply where the person intends to amend an approved research plan. <Amended on Mar. 30, 2021; Nov. 4, 2025>
1. Title of the research;
2. Purpose of and need for the research;
3. Contents and methods of the research;
4. Research period and schedule;
5. Expected effects of the research findings and ways of utilizing them.
